The thumbnail has `className="hidden ... lg:block"`, so it is `display: none` below the `lg` breakpoint. Browsers still fetch `<img>` elements that are `display: none` unless they are lazy-loaded, so every visible row fetches its post's feature image on mobile and tablet, where it is never shown.

The rows are virtualized, so the count is bounded, but the same images are fetched for every comment on a post and not deferred. Adding `loading="lazy"` keeps the fetch for off-screen and hidden images deferred. Rendering the element only at `lg` widths would avoid the fetch entirely.

::code{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="350-358"}

The comments output mapper is used for admin requests, members/public requests (the mapper branches on `utils.isMembersAPI(frame)`), and activity-feed comment events, which call `mapComment` directly. The new `feature_image` entry in `postFields` is applied to all of them. Every comment response now carries the post's feature image URL.

The URL is already public for published posts through the Content API, so this is not a secrets or access-control problem. Two points are worth confirming: the members-facing comments payload grows for every comment, and the public response is now changed even though only the admin list needs the image. If the intent is admin-only, gate the field on `!isPublicRequest`. The activity-feed change is a side effect that the snapshot update reflects (the `content-length` change), but the body snapshot is typed `Any<Object>`, so it doesn't pin the field.

